# Context handoff (Auto)

Chat memory ≠ SoT. Window thin, mid-step, or a new chat continues work → **files win**. Do not invent NEXT from residual chat.

Does **not** change Mode A/B STEP tokens (`00` / `08`). Halt strings stay exact.

## SoT (read first every continue / Scout)

1. `active_context.md` — Goal · Pins · Current slice · DONE / PARTIAL / NEXT · paste block
2. `progress.md` — inventory + slice status
3. User’s latest message (overrides stale file Status only when explicit)

If (1)+(2) contradict the latest user ask → **stop** · report drift · ask which wins. Do not implement.

## Automation (hooks — not a % meter)

Cursor **has no hook at 70%** (or any other percent). These project hooks fire instead:

| Event | Script | Does |
|-------|--------|------|
| `sessionStart` | `.cursor/hooks/session-start-sot.py` | Injects “read `active_context.md` + `progress.md`” into the new chat |
| `preCompact` | `.cursor/hooks/precompact-handoff-warn.py` | Compaction **already starting** — user warn + stamp `active_context` + `.cursor/compaction-pending.json`. **Cannot block** compact |
| `stop` | `.cursor/hooks/stop-handoff-nudge.py` | If pending signal exists, auto-submits **one** `handoff only` follow-up (`loop_limit: 1`) |

After a successful handoff refresh: delete the `<!-- compaction-signal -->` block in `active_context.md` and delete `.cursor/compaction-pending.json`.

Prefer refreshing handoff **before** compact (long thread / heavy tools). Do not wait for the hook.

## When to hard-stop (handoff only — no code)

Trigger any of:

- User: `context thin` · `handoff only` · `no code` · chat အသစ် / continue-from-files
- Self-check: long thread + large tool dumps + cannot restate DONE/NEXT from **files** without guessing
- Mid Mode B STEP 1/2/3 and the next action would require facts not in files or this turn’s tool results
- **`preCompact` signal** (warn, `active_context` Compaction signal block, or `.cursor/compaction-pending.json`) — treat as thin · handoff only (hook cannot block compact)

On hard-stop:

1. Update `active_context.md`: **DONE** · **PARTIAL** (if mid-STEP 3) · **NEXT** · **Out of scope** · paste-ready first message
2. Update `progress.md` if slice status changed
3. Reply: short status + paste block only — **no new code** · no STEP jump
4. End. Do not append “meanwhile I’ll also…”

## Mid-step partial

| State | Write to `active_context` |
|-------|---------------------------|
| STEP 1 done | Status = plan ready · NEXT = STEP 2 |
| STEP 2 done | NEXT = STEP 3 Implement |
| STEP 3 half-done | **PARTIAL** = files touched + what’s left · list exact paths |
| QA incomplete | PARTIAL = checks run / not run · NEXT = QA |

Never mark Visual / QA **PASS** without evidence in this turn or `progress.md`.

## Routine memory refresh

Treat file memory upkeep as part of the work, not an optional wrap-up.

- After any substantial scout, plan, implementation, QA result, or scope change, refresh `active_context.md` before ending the turn if DONE / PARTIAL / NEXT changed
- Update `progress.md` whenever slice status, inventory status, or suggested order meaningfully changes
- Before starting a new major task in the same chat, re-check whether `active_context.md` still matches reality; if stale, update it first
- If context usage is getting high or the thread is long, prefer a handoff refresh early instead of waiting for compaction
- Do not claim “already known” from chat memory alone when the same fact is missing or stale in files

## New chat / continue paste

Keep a fenced paste under `active_context.md` “Context ကုန်လို့ နောက် chat”:

```
Continue DBS-FFW from active_context.md + progress.md.
DONE: …
NEXT: …
Pins: SPFx 1.20 gulp, React 17, Fluent v8. Reject Heft/v9, classic master, secrets, Codegraph Cursor hooks.
If context thin: update active_context handoff only — no code.
Mode B: ..chain → y → y; one STEP per y.
```

New chat turn 1 = **Scout from files** (or handoff-only if user said so). Do not skip to Implement because “we were about to”.

## Reject

- Continuing from chat recall when `active_context` Status/NEXT is missing or stale
- Inventing PASS, video URLs, or “probably done”
- Expanding scope under thin context
- Replacing this rule with a Skill (session hygiene stays always-on `.mdc`)
- Writing to `~/.cursor/skills`
